hout, since BlackRock's OA rewards a fast brute force and finishing inside the clock over cleverness. No newly opened target roles today (only a non-target Bank of America listing; Trackr's live fetch was blocked again); JPMorgan Chase's two roles remain the nearest real published deadline behind BlackRock, at 57 days. Today's bar is non-negotiable: solve and log at least Valid Parentheses and Two Sum — the two easiest of today's set — because four days out from a real test with zero logged reps is the actual emergency now, not which topic gets drilled next.\n> BlackRock coding test is in 4 days (Wed 9 Sep) — practice is pinned to it until it is sat. Clear the `assessment_*` lines in targets.yaml afterwards.\n> Confirm the platform and time limit from the invite email and correct practice/assessments.yaml if it differs — the profile there assumes HackerRank, ~90 min.\n> Only 19 LeetCode problems are tagged BlackRock — enough to aim with, not enough to call a pattern. The rest of today's set matches its topic mix rather than claiming it was asked.\n> Most of it sits at easy/low-medium: hidden test cases and finishing inside the clock decide it, not clever algorithms. Get a brute force passing first, then optimise. Expect a finance-flavoured framing (prices, orders, time series) over plain arrays — read the prompt twice before typing."
